        "dimension": "OBJECT",
        "relation": "UNKNOWN",
        "source_value": "The authors give a multinomial expression for the stabilizer partition function of n copies of a single-qubit pure state, with a closed expression for T-state copies, and claim that T-state copies are distinguished from stabilizer states for every nonzero beta. This is an unverified author-claim candidate.",
        "target_value": "The authors state \\(\\mathcal Z_\\beta(\\psi^{\\otimes n})=e^{-\\beta}\\sum_{w=0}^n\\binom nw\\sum_{n_x,n_y,n_z}\\binom{w}{n_x\\,n_y\\,n_z}\\cosh(\\beta V_\\psi[\\vec n]),\\quad V_\\psi[\\vec n]=\\prod_{\\sigma\\in\\{X,Y,Z\\}}\\langle\\sigma\\rangle^{n_\\sigma}\\). For T copies they state \\(\\mathcal Z_\\beta(T^{\\otimes n})=e^{-\\beta}[(4^n-3^n)+\\sum_{k=0}^n\\binom nk2^k\\cosh(\\beta2^{-k/2})]\\), \\(\\mathcal Z_0=4^n\\), and \\(\\mathcal Z_\\beta(T^{\\otimes n})<\\mathcal Z_\\beta(\\mathrm{STAB}_n)\\) for nonzero beta.",
